WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
- So originally you were like
an athlete from Hong Kong?

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.510
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.343
- [Kelly] Like, fencing?

00:00:04.343 --> 00:00:05.297
- Yeah, I was a fencer.

00:00:05.297 --> 00:00:06.440
I was a fencer.
- Cool.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.500
- That's cool.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.680
- My parents, they were Olympians too.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.650
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Yeah,

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.200
my dad is a fencer and my mom's a gymnast.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.130
- Wow, so I guess it
would've been a let down

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.927
if you didn't do something
in that category.

00:00:17.927 --> 00:00:19.600
(all laughing)
- Yes, I mean,

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.522
I was prepping for
London Olympics back then

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:26.207
and then while prepping
I just told my parents,

00:00:26.207 --> 00:00:27.040
"Hey, you know what,

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.320
I always had this dream about music.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.950
Let me do my thing and-"

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.020
- How did that go over (laughs)?

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.810
- I mean, they want me of
course to go to the Olympics,

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:37.780
you know, do my thing.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.840
And it took me seven
months to persuade them.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.180
- Wow, but you were persistent.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.013
That's a lot of months.

00:00:43.013 --> 00:00:44.790
- Yeah, they were really against me.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.650
And then they're like,
"You're outta your mind."

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.140
My principal told me that,

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.010
this is the worst,

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.595
worst decision you're gonna
ever make in your life.

00:00:51.595 --> 00:00:52.587
- [Kelly] Have you sent him a letter?

00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:53.670
- No, no, no.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.760
- I think he knows by now he was wrong.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.966
- [Kelly] Or like a signed headshot.

00:00:57.966 --> 00:01:00.730
- Then after I debut as a singer

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:04.180
and I went back to have a
concert and I invited him.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.131
And then he said, "Jackson,
we believed in you."

00:01:07.131 --> 00:01:09.463
(all laughing)
Hey, we believed in you.

00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:12.160
- This happens, it happens.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:12.993
That happened to me.

00:01:12.993 --> 00:01:14.460
I was like, "What?"

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.147
People were totally like,

00:01:17.147 --> 00:01:19.340
"That's never gonna happen,
everybody has a dream."

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.330
And then they were like, "The whole time,"

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.777
you'd see them on news and they're like,

00:01:22.777 --> 00:01:24.200
"We believed from the beginning."

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.033
And I'm like,

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.380
"You are a liar."
- We knew you were the one.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.263
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.950
So, wait, were your parents
worried about you guys

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:31.783
in the entertainment industry?

00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:32.690
Were they worried?

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.167
- Yeah, at first I said,

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:37.560
"Hey, I passed this audition in Korea.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.200
I'm going, I'm leaving."

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.770
And then they're like, "You know what..."

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.847
They told me about this, like,

00:01:41.847 --> 00:01:43.700
"Entertainment, no
they're gonna kidnap you

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.258
and put you in a cave and-"

00:01:45.258 --> 00:01:46.112
- (laughs) Wait.
- What?

00:01:46.112 --> 00:01:47.560
- They're gonna do this,
yeah, like, parents.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.393
- Yeah.

00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:51.320
- And then they're like, "No,
you're not gonna do that.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.780
We're not gonna see you again.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.270
You're gonna be MIA."

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:58.990
And I'm like, "No, let me live my dream."

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:01.718
And, yeah, seven month of persuading them

00:02:01.718 --> 00:02:02.980
and they're supportive.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.300
- That's amazing.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.821
- Do we have to sit this far?

00:02:05.821 --> 00:02:07.335
(Natasha laughs)
- (indistinct) Sit here.

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:08.920
You're just so cool,
we're giving you room.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.238
- We wanna adopt him.

00:02:10.238 --> 00:02:12.502
(audience laughing)

00:02:12.502 --> 00:02:13.335
- Come here, come here.

00:02:13.335 --> 00:02:14.780
- [Kelly] We're giving you room.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.863
- Nobody's gonna kidnap you, son.

00:02:17.762 --> 00:02:18.625
- [Kelly] You are not-
- There's no caves for you.

00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:19.718
- [Kelly] You are not going-
- You made it, kid.

00:02:19.718 --> 00:02:21.581
- [Kelly] To a cave.
- You made it, kid.

